.TH RASKOLNIKOV 1 "2026-07-25" "raskolnikov 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
raskolnikov, rsk, rk \- terminal-native AI security operating environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raskolnikov
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR model ]
.RB [ \-\-provider
.IR provider ]
.br
.B rsk
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rk
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B raskolnikov
.B sessions
.IR action
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B raskolnikov
.B config
.RB [ show | provider | model | set
.IR key value ]
.br
.B raskolnikov
.B tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Raskolnikov
is a terminal-native, markdown-driven AI security operating environment for authorised penetration testing and CTF competitions.
It provides an interactive TUI with AI-powered analysis, tool integration, and session management.
.PP
The commands
.BR rsk (1)
and
.BR rk (1)
are symlinks to
.BR raskolnikov (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " model"
Override the default AI model for this session.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " provider"
Override the default AI provider for this session.
Valid values:
.BR auto ", " ollama ", " anthropic ", " openai ", " openrouter ", " groq ", " nous ", " llama-api ", " together .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS sessions
Manage past session data.
.TP
.B sessions list
List all saved sessions.
.TP
.B sessions show \fIID\fR
Show conversation transcript for session \fIID\fR.
.TP
.B sessions findings \fIID\fR
Show findings summary for session \fIID\fR.
.TP
.B sessions log \fIID\fR
Dump raw JSON session log for session \fIID\fR.
.TP
.BI sessions prune " [" --keep N | Nr ]
Remove old sessions.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B \-\-keep 30
(default): keep sessions from the last 30 days.
.IP \(bu 2
.B \-\-keep 10r
: keep the 10 most recent sessions.
.RE
.TP
.B sessions recover \fIID\fR
Recover \fIconversation.md\fR and \fIfindings.md\fR from \fIsession.log\fR.
.SS config
View or modify configuration.
.TP
.B config show
Display current configuration as TOML.
.TP
.BI config provider " name"
Set the AI provider.
.TP
.BI config model " name"
Set the default model.
.TP
.BI config set " key value"
Set an arbitrary config key. Supported keys:
.BR provider ", " model ", " ollama_host ", " nmap_timing ", " prefer_ffuf ", " sqlmap_level ", " sqlmap_risk ", " stream_output ", " alias ", " context_window ", " proxy ", " proxy_https ", " no_proxy ", " use_tmp_data_dir .
.SS tools
Check availability and versions of security tools (nmap, gobuster, nikto, sqlmap, hydra, whatweb, john, hashcat, feroxbuster, netexec, nuclei, enum4linux-ng, httpx).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in TOML format at:
.PP
.RS 4
~/.config/raskolnikov/config.toml
.RE
.PP
Override the path with the
.B RASKOLNIKOV_CONFIG
environment variable.
.PP
API keys are read from environment variables only:
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY ", " OPENROUTER_API_KEY ", " GROQ_API_KEY ", " NOUS_API_KEY ", " LLAMA_API_KEY ", " TOGETHER_API_KEY .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/raskolnikov/config.toml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/raskolnikov/sessions/
Session data directory (default). Override with
.B RASKOLNIKOV_DATA
or set
.B use_tmp_data_dir = true
in config.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RASKOLNIKOV_CONFIG
Override config file path.
.TP
.B RASKOLNIKOV_DATA
Override session data directory.
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY ", " etc.
API keys for cloud AI providers.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start with auto-detected provider:
.PP
.RS 4
raskolnikov
.RE
.PP
Start with a specific model:
.PP
.RS 4
raskolnikov \-\-model claude-sonnet-4-6 \-\-provider anthropic
.RE
.PP
Prune sessions older than 7 days:
.PP
.RS 4
rsk sessions prune \-\-keep 7
.RE
.PP
Keep only the 5 most recent sessions:
.PP
.RS 4
rk sessions prune \-\-keep 5r
.RE
